
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pronouns.mgr - Thai-pack first/second-person pronouns (Phase 8).
#
# Thai pronouns are gender- and formality-aware:
#   ฉัน (chan)    - first-person, neutral. Default for ?_I.
#   ผม (phom)     - first-person, masculine, polite. Accepts on parse.
#   ดิฉัน (dichan) - first-person, feminine, formal. Accepts on parse.
#   คุณ (khun)    - second-person, polite. Default for ?_you.
#   เธอ (thoe)    - second-person, intimate. Accepts on parse.
#
# Politeness ALSO rides on sentence-final particles (ครับ male / ค่ะ female)
# at the Statements.mgr level rather than on the pronoun itself. v1 emits
# ครับ as the polite-particle default - the speaker-gender split is a
# follow-up shared with Japanese 僕 / 私 selection (see phase8_design.md).
#
# Possessive forms in Thai are compositional - "X ของ <pronoun>" (X of-me).
# NounPhrases.mgr realizes that pattern; no separate possessive pronouns.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:PRONOUN

"ฉัน"      ?_I     .
"ผม"      ?_I     .
"ดิฉัน"     ?_I     .

"คุณ"      ?_you   .
"เธอ"      ?_you   .

"นี่"      ?_this  .
"นั่น"     ?_this  .
